		<notes>
			<note>This book and two similar "twelfth" editions, </note>
			<note url="games.3.p.2.xml">Games.3.P.2</note>
			<note> and </note>
			<note url="games.3.p.3.xml">Games.3.P.3</note>
			<note> are reprints of the authorized "twelfth" edition, </note>
			<note url="games.3.xml">Games.3</note>
			<note>. They have the same text, including the new material first added in </note>
			<note url="games.3.xml">Games.3</note>
			<note>, but omitting the material first added in the "thirteenth" edition, </note>
			<note url="games.4.xml">Games.4</note>
			<note>. Yet, there are important differences. The reprints lack to note "To the Reader" on the verso of the
				title page and are not autographed by Hoyle and Osborne. They are undoubtedly piracies. </note>
			<note rend="paragraph"/>
			<note>The reprints are duodecimos in sixes, while the authorized edition is in twelves. The errata
				on pages 212 and 214 of the original are corrected in the text of the three rerpints. The title page, a single leaf outside a
				gathering in the original (π1), is integral to the first gathering (A1), but the number of pages does
				not change because the three reprints omit the section title for whist. </note>
			<note rend="paragraph"/>
			<note>The four title pages are different settings of type. Indeed the type of each of the A through T
				gatherings is different from the authorized versions and from each other. With the exception of
				copies noted below, it appears that the reprints do not mix gatherings, that is </note>
			<note url="games.3.p.1.xml">Games.3.P.1</note>
			<note> always has one set of gatherings, </note>
			<note url="games.3.p.2.xml">Games.3.P.2</note>
			<note> another, and </note>
			<note url="games.3.p.3.xml">Games.3.P.3</note>
			<note> a third. </note>
			<note rend="paragraph"/>
			<note>The different setting of type are documented </note>
			<note url="../images/games.3.p-discussion.pdf">here</note>
			<note> and illustrated </note>
			<note url="../images/games.3.p-variants.pdf">here</note>
			<note>, both in PDF format.</note>
			<note rend="paragraph"/>
			<note>There are some oddities with gathering B. In O [Jessel f.558], CaOLU [GV1241.H8 copy 2],
				NvLN [GV1241 H69 1761?], TNJ [GV1241.H8 M12 c.2], and Levy [2212], gathering B is the type normally found in </note>
			<note url="games.3.p.2.xml">Games.3.P.2</note>
			<note>. Gathering B is missing altogether in Levy [1119]. </note>
		</notes>
